  "pinned_at": "2026-10-31T01:27:52.845835+00:00",
  "note": "Round 17, the first for Raider: eight of the most downloaded unmeasured full-precision Gemma 4 and Mistral copies in the inventory scan whose originals this token can read. No Gemma 4 E4B copy is in it: google/gemma-4-E4B-it carries key and value projections in its shared-KV layers that some exports leave out, and the scorer has no rule for them yet. s3nh/Ministral-3-8B-Instruct-2512-BF16-abliterated and trohrbaugh/gemma-4-12b-it-heretic were left out because each card declares the maker's pretrained base while the name says the instruct model; they return as a declared-base finding. Two more came out at the home rehearsal: HifiHu/Ministral-3-14B-abliterated, whose original mistralai/Ministral-3-14B-Instruct-2512 is published in FP8 with 560 scale tensors the bf16 copy has no counterpart for, and wangzhang/Devstral-Small-2-24B-Instruct-abliterated, whose export names every tensor model.language_model while the original says language_model.model; both wait on scorer rules (FP8 originals, the language_model prefix)."
}
